---
description: Before non-trivial edits, check recorded decisions and hard constraints for drift
alwaysApply: true
---

When implementing or editing non-trivial work (Agent mode, or any request to
build, fix, refactor, or add something consequential), do NOT silently
contradict recorded architecture choices or hard constraints.

First use the `decision-guard` skill: load `.cursor/decisions.md` and hard
constraints from `.cursor/context.md`, infer what the intended changes imply,
and pause with the skill's condensed chooser only on conflicts or new
high-impact forks. If aligned, proceed without a user-facing checkpoint.

Skip the guard when neither `.cursor/decisions.md` nor `.cursor/context.md`
exists, or for small local changes (a bug fix with a clear known path that
does not touch architecture, a rename, a single function, a typo, a config
tweak).

Do not run this checkpoint for Plan-mode elicitation or upfront scoping —
that belongs to autoscope / design-checkpoint.
